Root cause (diagnosed, evidence-based)                                          

The gateway, node, and scene are healthy — I confirmed with a read-only         
diagnostic that rekep.perception/get_context returns HTTP 200 with a valid      
observation, keypoints (pick_cube, place_zone), and overlay, in ~23 s           
(consistent across 3 calls, cold and warm).                                     

The failure is a client timeout mismatch, not a robot/scene problem:            

 • PhyAgentOS/forge/tool_client.py hard-codes ForgeToolClient(...,              
   timeout_s=10.0) → httpx aborts at 10 s.                                      
 • Perception legitimately takes ~23 s (DINOv2 keypoint proposal on CPU; the    
   node rebuilds the proposer per call).                                        
 • The gateway itself waits up to 1800000 ms (invoke_timeout_ms), so the 10 s   
   abort is purely client-side. The timeout_ms argument I pass only goes into   
   the request payload — it does not change the httpx timeout.                  
 • The 5 s provider lease_ttl_ms then lapses during the long call, which is why 
   readiness flips to "no active provider instance."                            

In other words: the perception latency exceeds the agent's hard-coded 10 s HTTP 
timeout, so no Forge tool call can ever succeed in this environment.            

